### Step 1: Bug Scenario Image Description & Root Cause Reasoning

**Bug Scenario Image Description:**
- The image shows the Prettier playground with a code sample: a directive (`'use strict';`), a blank line, and a comment (`// comment`).
- The left side is the input, the right side is the output.
- The output has an **extra blank line** at the end (two newlines after the comment), which is not expected.

**Root Cause Reasoning:**
- The bug report and image indicate that when a file contains a directive followed by a comment, Prettier outputs two trailing newlines instead of one.
- The bug is specific to the Babylon parser and occurs when the file structure is: directive → blank line → comment.
- The root cause is likely in the logic that determines when to add a trailing newline at the end of the file, specifically in the `"Program"` node handling in the printer.

### Step 2: Bug Code Snippet Analysis & Bug Location

- The relevant code is in `src/language-js/printer-estree.js`, specifically in the `"Program"` case of the `printPathNoParens` function.
- The code currently adds a `hardline` (newline) at the end if there are any contents or comments:
  ```js
      // Only force a trailing newline if there were any contents.
      if (
        !n.body.every(({ type }) => type === "EmptyStatement") ||
        n.comments
